sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor F as Finance desk
    actor A as Administrator
    actor S as Student
    participant FI as finance-service
    participant K as Kafka
    participant NO as notification-service

    F->>FI: POST /api/fees/refunds (payment, amount, reason)
    FI->>FI: refuse if the payment was reversed, or the amount is more than is left to refund (less requests still pending)
    FI->>K: notify the administrator (Refund to approve)

    alt Administrator approves
        A->>FI: POST /api/fees/refunds/{id}/approve
        FI->>FI: lock the payment, add the amount to refunded_amount
        FI->>FI: paid = payment - refunded, so the plan owes the money again (SETTLED to ACTIVE)
        FI->>K: notify the student by email and in the portal (Refund approved)
        K->>NO: queue the email
    else Administrator rejects
        A->>FI: POST /api/fees/refunds/{id}/reject (reason)
        FI->>FI: status REJECTED, nothing changes on the payment
    end

    Note over F,FI: The money is handed back outside the system, then recorded
    F->>FI: POST /api/fees/refunds/{id}/paid (cash, UPI, bank transfer or cheque, reference, date)
    FI->>FI: refuse a date inside a closed period
    FI->>FI: status PAID with how, when and by whom
    FI->>FI: a cash refund lowers that day's expected cash in the day-end count
    FI->>K: notify the student (Refund paid)

    opt Credit note
        F->>FI: GET /api/fees/refunds/{id}/credit-note (or the student, their own)
        FI->>FI: the tax of the original receipt, in proportion to the refund
        FI-->>F: PDF: credit note no, the receipt it credits, taxable value, CGST and SGST or IGST, reason
    end
